Since the game jam theme is "bounce back", we wanted to take that in two differernt ways. One is to bounce back in time, from the present to ancient Rome.
The other way we took "bounce back" is real bouncing, bullet bouncing. 
Our game is about a priest bounced back in time, trying to cleasnse the sins of ancient Romes gladiators. 
The priest has a gun, loaded with holy water. These bullets bounce off walls and enemies, doing damage. 
The gladiators spawn around the priest, in an attempt to kill him, as he is in their collosseum. 
Defeating gladiators grants score, and they sometimes drop extra ammo.
The priest has an ability, triggered by pressing space. It slows down the time of the bullets fired in the time, and cancelling the ability causes the buildup
of bullets to fire all at once. This ability has a cooldown. 
The game gets harder as the preist defeats enemies.
Controls
WASD is used to move, with forward being where the cursor is. Looking up and pressing W goes up, looking right and pressing D goes down. 
Left click to shoot, right click and R are reload. 
Space to activate special ability. 
